				(property "Datasheet" "https://www.raspberrypi.com/documentation/computers/raspberry-pi.html"
					(at 0 0 0)
					(show_name no)
					(do_not_autoplace no)
					(hide yes)
					(effects
						(font
							(size 1.27 1.27)
						)
					)
				)
				(property "Description" "Raspberry Pi 40-pin GPIO header (Model B+ onward, incl. Pi 5). Pinout verified against the published GPIO connector table. On the V3 carrier this is mainly the 5V feed from A2 (Pololu D36V50F5, 5.5A) plus a UART/I2C link to the Teensy - navigation and CV stay on the Pi, the Teensy is the real-time executor. NOTE: in the V2 bench the GPS sat on GPIO15 (/dev/ttyAMA0 @38400) and the A4988 stepper on the Pi header; in V3 both move to the Teensy, so those pins are free. A Pi 5 draws up to 5A on its own - budget the rail accordingly."
					(at 0 0 0)
					(show_name no)
					(do_not_autoplace no)
					(hide yes)
					(effects
						(font
							(size 1.27 1.27)
						)
					)
